{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-14T05:21:52.343Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"59bab72f78a0d9fe45da6dce","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/6","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-14T05:21:52.342Z","author":"pi-agent","text":"CodeQL js/polynomial-redos alert #18 on the brace-union regex introduced by this PR: the leftmost-union exec() backtracks polynomially, and measurements confirm it (adversarial '{{,' + 50k commas takes ~19.4 s; the 200k variant exceeds 100 s). Plan: replace the regex with a single-pass indexOf/char scanner that keeps the exact leftmost expandable-union semantics (nested and non-comma braces untouched, same left-to-right expansion order), bound expansion at 1024 alternatives with a clear refusal error so hostile configured globs cannot explode memory, document the limit in the docstring and README, add adversarial timing, expansion-limit and semantics tests, and record a behavioural revert proof."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-14T05:21:52.343Z"}],"before_hash":"d6d54b14741c5ef817463ed6e9354bd99fd2b03c61f2d4d751df447e03a591d5","after_hash":"69379e8c272e55b69aef50f72568143fd49ee754d923fcebca126f7ec6dcc668","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"979c380675a45eb3660aef6d0a83e36387bab2c3489db8d4737700843f53f468"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-14T05:27:21.829Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"59bab72f78a0d9fe45da6dce","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/7","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-14T05:27:21.829Z","author":"pi-agent","text":"Revert proof (behavioural): with only expandGlobUnions restored to the flagged regex body, the new tests fail exactly as required — the adversarial timing test takes 20.6 s (50 ms bound; the 200k-comma variant exceeds 100 s) and the expansion-refusal test fails because the unbounded regex silently expands past 1024 alternatives. With the linear scanner restored, the same suite passes: the '{{,' + 50k-commas input expands in ~0.2 ms and the closing-brace variant refuses in ~0.3 ms. Semantics were also differentially verified: the scanner and the old regex produce identical expansions for 400,000 random patterns (including nested, non-comma, empty-alternative and negative-alternative braces)."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-14T05:27:21.829Z"}],"before_hash":"69379e8c272e55b69aef50f72568143fd49ee754d923fcebca126f7ec6dcc668","after_hash":"47f333eb7ea61be62808af515c170c6d51431d1ec9817857d65e7e3a1524381a","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"4571034d8d002f3a902ea97122aafab7fe6c20a84fc4dac7d6c9cbc1b1bcb4bc"}
